### Phase 2 — Query Invocation (run-time)
### Lets you call a published query and watch the response in the IDE's HTTP client.
### Prereqs: query_engine is running (./dry-run.sh) and
### orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch has been published (run publish_query.http, or
### frontend_service once).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Invoke the published query by its namespaced name, with a role allowed to call it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### Same call, bare name (unambiguous short name also resolves).
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: chief_DBA

{
  "name": "ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### 403 FORBIDDEN — caller's role is not in allowed_roles for this query.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: support_agent

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT — missing a required param.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED"
  }
}

### 404 QUERY_NOT_FOUND — nothing published under this name.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.doesNotExist",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### Sanity check: list published/drafted queries (Phase 1 endpoint) to see what's available to call.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/list
Content-Type: application/json

{}
